      "text": "Hello there, how are you doing today?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 8.36,
      "end": 14.82,
      "text": "For acrylics, rinse them in water while you work, then wash with mild soap at the end. Don't let paint dry in the bristles."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 18.53,
      "end": 22.8,
      "text": "That bends the tips and loosens the glue in the handle. Lay them flat to dry instead."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 25.44,
      "end": 31.18,
      "text": "Sometimes. Soak them in a bit of rubbing alcohol or a proper brush restorer, then work the paint out gently."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 33.67,
      "end": 38.19,
      "text": "Keep them for rough jobs like texture or dry brushing. Old brushes are great for that."
    }
  ]
